        "id": 9332,
        "name": "torian",
        "username": "torian",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/919ad9/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-28T18:36:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;A co-worker and I have been having a discussion today, I've looked around the forums and could not find an answer. The premiss goes like this: Say I play 'Nimble Strike' and my only available target has damage reduction 1, negating my damage. Am I still able to draw a card?</p><p><span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Another example would be 'Motivation Charge': If Damage reduction or immunity negates the two damage, do the heroes still regain 1 HP?</span></p><p><span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;His arguement is that for nimble strike a card is still drawn because the wording on the card is 'may draw a card' and that the heroes do not regain HP because he feels the HP recovery is linked to the damage. I argue both post damage effects occur, but do not have any backup besides there is nothing in the rules that say the effects are linked and it limits options for low damage characters with similar powers that go up against villains with damage reduction.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:05.736Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
