        "id": 87794,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-28T19:29:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If the effects are separate grammatically, then their effects aren't linked and being stopped from doing one doesn't stop the other.&nbsp; As Braithwaite says, with Nimble Strike, you'll deal the damage (period).&nbsp; Next, you'll draw a card (period).&nbsp; If the card was worded so that you \"deal 1 target 1 melee damage, then draw a card\" and you were prevented from doing the damage, then the linked part about drawing a card would also be prevented.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:12:11.667Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 9331,
        "topic_slug": "effects-attached-to-damage-vs-damage-reduction",
        "display_username": "Spiff",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
