        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>If the effects are separate grammatically, then their effects aren&#39;t linked and being stopped from doing one doesn&#39;t stop the other.&nbsp; As Braithwaite says, with Nimble Strike, you&#39;ll deal the damage (period).&nbsp; Next, you&#39;ll draw a card (period).&nbsp; If the card was worded so that you &quot;deal 1 target 1 melee damage, then draw a card&quot; and you were prevented from doing the damage, then the linked part about drawing a card would also be prevented.</p>",
