        "raw": "[quote=\"Spiff\"]\n\nIf the effects are separate grammatically, then their effects aren&#39;t linked and being stopped from doing one doesn&#39;t stop the other.&nbsp; As Braithwaite says, with Nimble Strike, you&#39;ll deal the damage (period).&nbsp; Next, you&#39;ll draw a card (period).&nbsp; If the card was worded so that you &quot;deal 1 target 1 melee damage, then draw a card&quot; and you were prevented from doing the damage, then the linked part about drawing a card would also be prevented.\n\n[/quote]\n\nJust a clarification Spiff, the wording would have to be &quot;deal target X damage, then,&nbsp;<strong><em>if you do</em></strong>, carry out effect Z&quot;. The word &quot;then&quot; just implies order, it does not imply dependence.\n\n@ OP, any secondary effect that is&nbsp;<em>dependent</em> upon the initial effect will be worded that way in the sentence. You will get a feel for it as you compare effects and abilities across the game.\n\n Another quick note on Hypersonic Assult: The secondary effect is dependant upon the first, so damage must get through, but it takes effect as soon as damage is done. So if you are facing Matriarch for example, when you play Hypersonic, ping Matriarch first, apply the debuff,  <em>then</em>  kill all the birds since Matty is prevented from dealing her retaliation damage \n",
