      {
        "id": 87797,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-29T02:09:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It can be a bit tricky to figure out how some card text should be interpreted, given that you are sometimes expected to stop resolving rules text <em>in mid-sentence</em> (the classic example being Wrest the Mind...if Visionary kills the Wrested target with damage, she never deals any to herself), while other times, a card stays in play long enough to apply a when-destroyed effect (e.g. Sonic Mine or Explosives Wagon).&nbsp; In most cases, common sense is the correct answer, but this isn't always 100% reliable.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:12:11.907Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 9331,
        "topic_slug": "effects-attached-to-damage-vs-damage-reduction",
        "display_username": "Envisioner",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
